---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Grok Bot" description="What Grok Bot is: AI teammates that can use tools and return finished work.">
  <section class="about-content">
    <p class="home-kicker" style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Features</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Grok Bot</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle muted">AI teammates that act with tools, not only chat.</p>
    <p><strong>Grok Bot</strong> is xAI's name for agent-style teammates built on Grok models. Official descriptions emphasise teammates that can sign into tools, perform real work, and return finished results.</p>
    <h2>From early beta to public beta</h2>
    <p>xAI first described Grok Bot in an early beta context, then moved it into a broader public beta. Grokati tracks those stage changes because they matter for availability.</p>
    <h2>What Grok Bot is for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Delegating multi-step tasks rather than only asking one-off questions</li>
      <li>Working with tools and accounts the bot can sign into</li>
      <li>Receiving finished outputs instead of only suggestions</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Grok Bot vs models and Grok Build</h2>
    <p><a href="/models">Models</a> are the intelligence. Grok Bot is a product experience on top. <a href="/build">Grok Build</a> is a related harness aimed at coding and long-running agentic work.</p>
    <p>In short: model = brain, Bot = teammate product, Build = development/evaluation harness.</p>
    <h2>How Grokati covers Grok Bot</h2>
    <p>Beta openings, access changes, and official capability statements appear under the Grok Bot category.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 2rem;"><a href="/features">← All features</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>